Horology-Hulk

Creative Catalyst: The instruments are forged from star-fallen meteoric iron bonded to the recalcitrant guts of 18th-century pendulum clocks.

Horology-Hulk is the sound of celestial entropy meeting mechanical fury. It utilizes the Shreddamage 3 Hydra to generate sub-harmonic chugs that oscillate at the exact resonant frequency of falling stone. The audio texture is characterized by "Gear-Grind Clipping," where the metallic fatigue of the clockwork components creates natural, non-algorithmic distortion. It sounds like a landslide occurring inside a brass pipe organ, punctuated by the rhythmic, teeth-shattering precision of 2010s-era djent architecture.

Genre DNA
*   Tempo & Pulse: 175–210 BPM, utilizing poly-rhythmic "ticking" shuffles that break into erratic, gravity-defying blasts.
*   Harmonic Palette: Diminished-Phrygian and microtonal "corroded" scales; favors dissonance over resolution.
*   Production Signatures: Direct-to-tape meteorite-induction recording, "Torsion Limiting" (capping volume via actual physical clock-spring resistance), and phase-shifted clockwork percussion.
*   Dynamics: Abrupt transitions between hyper-compressed silence and chaotic, tectonic wall-of-sound swells.

Scene & Origin Lore
Born in the high-altitude industrial ruins of the Andes, the Horology-Hulk scene emerged in 2014 when a rogue collective of horologists and metalcore refugees synthesized their crafts. They worship at the altar of the Iron Second, a ritual involving the mass synchronization of antique pendulum movements until they harmonize with the 8-string Hydra’s lower F# strings. Members dress in "Shattered-Formal" wear—victorian suits woven with meteoritic filament—and perform under a vow of silence, communicating only through percussive taps and the screech of gear-work. Their concerts are illicit, held in deep-earth bunkers where the ambient pressure ensures the instruments remain in perfect, volatile tension.

Primary Instruments: Shreddamage 3 Hydra 8-string djent machine, antique cast-iron escapement wheels, amplified pendulum weights, and magnetic induction pickups harvested from fallen impact sites.

For Fans Of: Meshuggah, Dillinger Escape Plan, Igorrr, and Hella.

