Track 2: "Where are the springs kept?"
- Story & Context: Silas the horologist stood at the edge of the abandoned canyon known as Dead-Man’s Latitude, holding a rusted key while his hands trembled with the vibration of the subterranean rhythm. A sudden gear-shift from the deep earth caused the canyon wall to collapse, crushing his watchmaker’s stool and sealing the history of their guild in stone. He screamed the question into the dust: "Tell me, where are the springs kept?" while the Hydra erupted into a stuttering, polyrhythmic breakdown that mimicked a failing machine.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A lonely figure clutching a burning golden key amidst a wall of collapsing gears and boulders, hyper-realistic dust and debris, cinematic lighting.

Track 3: The Rust-Eater's Lament
- Story & Context: Long after the village of New Tundra burned, the survivors whispered of the Rust-Eater, a spirit who consumed all recorded time left behind in the cinders. He wanders the perimeter of the ghost town, his heavy metallic boots clanking in 17/8 time against the frost-covered permafrost. "Consume the hours before they rust" he whispers, as the entire mountain seems to vibrate with the force of his hunger, blending clockwork chimes into a wall of crushing djent distortion.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A faceless silhouette standing on a barren hill surrounded by millions of tiny frozen gears, a galaxy of falling stars above, deep indigo and rusted orange color palette.

